# Database Schema & Controller Analysis

This document provides a comprehensive overview of the database structure (Firestore collections) and their relationships within the **Fean Pet Shop** backend.

## 1. Database Collections (Tables)

Since this project uses **Firebase Firestore**, data is stored in "Collections" rather than traditional SQL tables. Each document in a collection represents a record.

### Collections Overview

| Collection | Description | Primary Controller |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `users` | Stores user profiles, authentication metadata, and roles. | [userController.js](file:///c:/Users/Samar%20Taibani/Desktop/fean/backend/controllers/userController.js), [authController.js](file:///c:/Users/Samar%20Taibani/Desktop/fean/backend/controllers/authController.js) |
| `products` | Contains details of pets and pet food items. | [productController.js](file:///c:/Users/Samar%20Taibani/Desktop/fean/backend/controllers/productController.js) |
| `categories` | Categorizes products (e.g., Dog Food, Cats). | [categoryController.js](file:///c:/Users/Samar%20Taibani/Desktop/fean/backend/controllers/categoryController.js) |
| `orders` | Records transactions and order status tracking. | [orderController.js](file:///c:/Users/Samar%20Taibani/Desktop/fean/backend/controllers/orderController.js) |
| `payments` | Stores detailed payment transaction history. | [paymentController.js](file:///c:/Users/Samar%20Taibani/Desktop/fean/backend/controllers/paymentController.js) |
| `wishlist` | Tracks products users have saved for later. | [wishlistController.js](file:///c:/Users/Samar%20Taibani/Desktop/fean/backend/controllers/wishlistController.js) |
| `ratings` | Stores product reviews and star ratings. | [ratingController.js](file:///c:/Users/Samar%20Taibani/Desktop/fean/backend/controllers/ratingController.js) |
| `contacts` | Stores messages from the "Contact Us" form. | [contactController.js](file:///c:/Users/Samar%20Taibani/Desktop/fean/backend/controllers/contactController.js) |

---

## 2. Key Fields & Data Structure

### `users`
- `uid`: Unique User ID (from Firebase Auth)
- `email`: User's email address
- `role`: `0` for User, `1` for Admin
- `name`, `phone`, `address`: Basic profile info
- `profileImage`: URL to the user's avatar
- `addresses`: Array of saved delivery addresses

### `products`
- `id`: Unique Product ID
- `type`: `pet` or `food`
- `name`, `description`, `price`, `stock`
- `categoryId`: Reference to the `categories` collection
- `images` (Array) / `imageUrl`: Product visuals
- **Pet Specific**: `breed`, `lifeExpectancy`, `careInstructions`
- **Food Specific**: `companyName`, `expiryDate`, `weight`, `flavor`

### `orders`
- `userId`: Reference to the user who placed the order
- `items`: Array of objects containing `productId`, `quantity`, `price`, `name`
- `totalAmount`: Sum of all items
- `status`: `Pending`, `Shipped`, `Delivered`, `Cancelled`, `Collected`
- `paymentStatus`: `Paid` or `Pending`
- `shippingDetails`: `address`, `phone`, `customerName`, `email`

---

## 3. Entity Relationship (ER) Diagram

Below is a technical representation of the connections between these entities.

```mermaid
erDiagram
    USERS ||--o{ ORDERS : places
    USERS ||--o{ WISHLIST : maintains
    USERS ||--o{ RATINGS : writes
    USERS ||--o{ PAYMENTS : makes

    PRODUCTS ||--o{ ORDERS : "contained in"
    PRODUCTS ||--o{ WISHLIST : "saved in"
    PRODUCTS ||--o{ RATINGS : "rated in"

    CATEGORIES ||--o{ PRODUCTS : categorizes

    ORDERS ||--o| PAYMENTS : "has record"
    
    USERS {
        string uid PK
        string email
        int role
        string name
        string profileImage
    }

    PRODUCTS {
        string id PK
        string name
        string type
        float price
        int stock
        string categoryId FK
    }

    CATEGORIES {
        string id PK
        string name
    }

    ORDERS {
        string id PK
        string userId FK
        float totalAmount
        string status
        string paymentStatus
    }

    RATINGS {
        string id PK
        string userId FK
        string productId FK
        int rating
        string comment
    }
```

---

## 4. Relationship Logic

1.  **Product - Category**: Each product belongs to one category. If a category is deleted, products under it may lose their context.
2.  **Order - User**: Every order is linked to a `uid`. This allows users to see their "My Orders" history.
3.  **Order - Product**: An order contains multiple items. Each item references a `productId` to fetch current name/images for display.
4.  **Rating/Wishlist**: These are "Bridge" collections that link a [User](file:///c:/Users/Samar%20Taibani/Desktop/fean/backend/controllers/userController.js#85-99) to a [Product](file:///c:/Users/Samar%20Taibani/Desktop/fean/backend/controllers/productController.js#50-106).

